      "id": "std86vz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: BASIC CONCEPT OF UNEMPLOYMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Unemployment is categorized into seven major types: Open, Disguised, Seasonal, Structural, Cyclical, Educated, and Technological.",
        "Disguised unemployment is characterized by zero marginal productivity of labor, heavily affecting the agricultural sector.",
        "Structural unemployment results from a long-term mismatch between available job skills and market requirements.",
        "The causes and effects of unemployment span both economic and social dimensions, requiring targeted policy responses.",
        "Addressing unemployment in India relies on government measures, policy interventions, and accelerating overall economic growth."
      ],
      "id": "4vbfzrj"
    },
